          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "બગડવું (bagaḍvũ) goes back to Sanskrit vighaṭatē, \"flies apart, is marred, is broken\", but CDIAL marks the Gujarati verb, glossed \"to be spoilt\", as borrowed from Hindi (CDIAL 11673)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
